<title>PORTUGAL: Drivers' strike brings Portuguese trains to a halt.</title>
<headline>Drivers' strike brings Portuguese trains to a halt.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese international and mainline trains came to a standstill on Friday as train drivers began a week-long strike, a spokesman for Portuguese railways said.</p>
<p>&quot;We're trying to keep suburban services running but not with the usual frequency,&quot; he said. He said some regional trains were running but with delays.</p>
<p>It was unclear how many of the 1,570 drivers had joined the strike to press for improved working conditions.</p>
<p>Portuguese railways, Caminhos de Ferros Portugueses (CP), runs international passenger services to Spain and France.</p>
</text>
